    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start for the kids. To make it a bit more impactful, can you add a section that highlights why this is considered the most important way the court protects people from unfair laws? Maybe contrast it with just following \"procedures\" so they see why substantive due process is the real hero in these civil rights cases.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The true power of substantive due process is that it addresses the *content* of the law, not just *how* the law is enforced. While procedural due process only requires fair *rules* for the government to follow, substantive due process challenges the law itself if it is fundamentally unjust or oppressive. This is the \"hero\" aspect because it allows the Supreme Court to declare an unfair law unconstitutional, even if the government followed all the correct legal steps in passing it. In civil rights, this is what truly overturns biased legislation that the \"process\" would have otherwise legitimized.",
      "source": "target",
