    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I think some of my more skeptical students might argue that judges using \"substantive due process\" to overturn laws is actually just them making up their own rules and acting like a \"super legislature\" rather than following the Constitution. How would you address those critics who say this doctrine is just an excuse for judicial activism?",
